WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.550
Harley Quinn's popularity is a fairly recent
phenomenon, so you might not remember the

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.400
finer details of her backstory.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.120
But with Birds of Prey hitting cinemas and
a new Suicide Squad on the horizon, now is

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.740
as good a time as any to bone up on Harley's
dark and checkered past.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.100
Harley Quinn is a member of a short list of
comic book characters who weren't adapted

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.660
from page to screen, but actually went about
it the other way around.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:28.220
The character first appeared in "Joker's Favor,"
a 1992 episode of Batman: The Animated Series.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.300
Throughout the show, she made regular appearances
as a henchwoman obsessed with the Joker, and

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.130
the Clown Prince of Crime clearly doesn't
reciprocate her feelings.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.800
"The babies!

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.800
We can’t leave the babies!

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.480
“I’ll buy you a goldfish let's go!"

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.440
Animated Series writer Paul Dini conceived
of Harley Quinn while watching his old college

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.080
friend Arleen Sorkin on Days of Our Lives.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.420
Sorkin dressed as a joker in a dream sequence
for the soap, and the scene inspired Dini

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.620
to not only create Joker's twisted girlfriend
but to hire Sorkin to voice her.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.360
Sorkin went on to play Quinn on numerous projects
over the following decades, most recently

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.439
for the online roleplaying game DC Universe
Online.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.760
Speaking about her character to Starlog Magazine,
Sorkin said:

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.300
"She wants to be a good girl, but it's so
much more her to be a bad one."

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.420
It would take seven years from her TV debut
for Harley Quinn to officially become part

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.060
of the DC Comics Universe.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.820
Quinn had previously appeared in comics, most
memorably in the 1994 64-page special The

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:31.639
Batman Adventures: Mad Love, which established
her origin as Joker's former doctor at Arkham

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.160
Asylum.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:36.320
But those comics were connected to the world
of the animated series, and they weren't part

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.160
of the larger DC Comics narrative.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.700
Harley's first canonical appearance in DC
comics came in 1999's Batman: Harley Quinn

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.469
#1, which made up part of the No Man's Land
event in which Gotham City is abandoned by

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:51.680
the US government after being nearly destroyed
by a massive earthquake.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.739
Like her counterpart in Mad Love, this Harley
was also Joker's doctor, and again she fell

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.060
for him in a big way.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.600
Harley helps Joker escape Arkham Asylum, gets
caught, and is immediately committed herself.

00:02:03.609 --> 00:02:07.969
When the events of No Man's Land enable all
the asylum's inmates to escape, Quinn finds

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:11.940
her jester get-up in an abandoned costume
store, and seeks out her lost love.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:16.720
Of course, Harley is as loyal as always, taking
on Penguin and his goons for Joker and later

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.960
going one-on-one with Batman so Joker can
make his escape.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:24.700
Obviously, Joker's reward is to trick her
into going inside a rocket which he then crashes

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.200
remotely.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.659
Harley survives, and it's Poison Ivy who finds
her and nurses her back to health, kicking

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.580
off a storied relationship for the comics
version of Harley.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.620
The first ongoing Harley Quinn comic premiered
in late 2000.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.659
In the first issue, Harley is still under
Joker's spell in spite of the abuse she's

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.840
endured by his hand.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:46.140
But eventually, with the help of Poison Ivy,
Harley manages to see enough of the real Joker

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.080
to rebel against him and his henchmen.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.580
Their renewed relationship ends with Harley
hurling the Clown Prince of Crime into a neon

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:53.080
sign.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:59.040
The series ended with 2004's Harley Quinn
#38, a story that left its hero with a bleak,

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:00.469
yet predictable, fate.

00:03:00.469 --> 00:03:04.489
The final issue ends with Harley deciding
she belongs back home and the penultimate

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:08.720
page shows Harley, in the pouring rain, pounding
on the doors of Arkham Asylum.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.940
In the last page's final panel, as Quinn is
led to her cell, her face breaks into a smile.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.960
In 2009, Harley Quinn made some friends.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.160
That year saw the debut of Gotham City Sirens
#1, in which Harley joins forces with fellow

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.360
female anti-heroes Catwoman and Poison Ivy.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.260
It all starts after Ivy saves Catwoman from
a supervillain wanna-be named Bonebreaker,

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.820
after which she invites Selina Kyle to her
new home the apartment of the Riddler, who

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:37.420
Ivy has rendered catatonic with her mind control
powers.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.120
And then Harley shows up shortly afterward,
announcing she's moving in.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:45.180
It's clear that, even after years of abuse
and multiple attempts to kill each other,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.240
Harley is still obsessed with the Joker.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:53.060
Shortly after arriving at Ivy's new pad, Harley
insists she's over "Mr. J," then seconds later,

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.420
excitedly asks if he's called.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.430
By the end of the issue, the three women have
agreed to join forces, and leave Riddler's

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.580
apartment for an abandoned animal shelter.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.480
Gotham City Sirens would only last 26 issues
but if nothing else, it marked an important

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.240
step in the evolution of Harley Quinn.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.879
After all, this series saw Harley's first
comics team-up with other women in lead roles,

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.680
a pattern that would be repeated throughout
the character's history.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:21.180
In August 2009, both DC fans and gamers alike
were treated to one of the franchise's best

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.700
ever video games Batman: Arkham Asylum.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:27.950
In this hit game, the player takes on the
role of Batman who, after delivering Joker

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.270
to the titular asylum, is forced to stop a
breakout conceived by the Clown Prince of

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:33.200
Crime himself.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.080
Naturally, Harley is all too happy to get
involved.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.640
"Bye bye for now!"

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:43.320
Harley appears a fair bit throughout the game,
though she's one of the only Bat-villains

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.140
that the player never confronts physically.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:49.960
After sending squads of thugs after the hero,
Harley is easily overpowered by Batman in

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:50.640
a cutscene.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.660
What's perhaps most significant about Harley's
spot in the game, however, is that it's her

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:58.220
first major appearance in media without her
classic jester suit.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:02.400
Instead, she wears a nurse outfit, sporting
the twin ponytails that would later become

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.600
a Harley Quinn staple.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.160
Believe it or not, Harley Quinn didn't appear
at all in the first three volumes of Suicide

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:08.660
Squad.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.260
But in the years since, she's since become
such an inseparable part of Task Force X that

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.740
it's difficult to imagine there was a time
when the team of villains could function without

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:17.240
her.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:22.640
Harley's 2011 debut in Suicide Squad came
as part of DC's line-wide reboot, The New

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:27.660
52, during which Harley's jester look was
abandoned for colorful ponytails and a much

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.620
skimpier outfit.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.470
Adam Glass wrote most of the first 19 issues
of the new volume, teaming Harley up with

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:39.020
Task Force X mainstays like Deadshot and Captain
Boomerang, as well as newer additions like

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.540
King Shark and Diablo.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:45.080
There have been two subsequent volumes of
Suicide Squad since the New 52 series ended

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:50.250
with its 30th issue, as well as the short-lived
New Suicide Squad, with Harley center-stage

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:50.800
at every turn.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.140
Girl loves the spotlight.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:57.280
Three years after the debut of the New 52,
Harley once again starred in her own solo

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:57.780
series.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.920
This time, Harley's story was co-written by
a team that has since become a fan-favorite:

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.000
Amanda Conner and Jimmy Palmiotti.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:09.000
These two writers arguably became so popular
because they knew just why people love Harley:

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.700
because she's fun.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:14.360
The series opens with Harley being willed
an entire apartment building on Coney Island

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.400
from an old patient.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.740
There she's joined by hilarious supporting
characters such as the ex-spy, Sy Borgman,

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.440
and the dead beaver Bernie who is in constant
contact with Harley despite, you know, being

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:25.940
dead.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.800
For a long time, there was rampant speculation
that Harley Quinn and fellow Gotham City anti-hero

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.440
Poison Ivy were more than just friends.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:38.530
They'd been trading innuendo and hints in
comics, cartoons, and even video games for

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:42.240
years, but it was a long time before there
was any kind of official word on the matter.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:47.320
However, writers Jimmy Palmiotti and Amanda
Conner confirmed Harley and Ivy's relationship

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.200
status in 2015.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:55.500
And in 2017's Harley Quinn #25, fans finally
got to see these two characters share a kiss.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:07:01.020
Sadly, Ivy's unexpected death in the 2018
mini-series Heroes in Crisis is part of what

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:05.139
drives Harley over the edge and again puts
her on a collision course with a group of

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.960
heroes including Batman and Booster Gold.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.120
Thankfully, this isn't the end of Ivy.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.039
By the end of the series, it's discovered
that Ivy prepared for her death by creating

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.740
a plant-based clone of herself.

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:20.980
Since then, Harley and the new Ivy have teamed
up for the 2019 Harley Quinn and Poison Ivy

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:21.660
miniseries.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:26.939
In 2016, Harley Quinn finally made her way
to the big screen sporting a baseball bat

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.700
and short shorts combo in David Ayer's Suicide
Squad.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.100
Rising star Margot Robbie was cast in the
role of the mentally unhinged Quinn, after

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:38.280
impressing critics and audiences with her
performance in Martin Scorsese's The Wolf

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.000
of Wall Street.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.720
Amidst an ensemble cast, including superstar
Will Smith, Viola Davis and Jared Leto, Robbie's

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.930
version of Harley was a genuine standout.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:50.200
"I'm known to be vexing I’m just warning
you.”

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.160
“Lady shut up!"

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:57.020
Of course, it's no secret that Suicide Squad
wasn't exactly a favorite of the critics.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.949
But even the critics who couldn't stand the
movie as a whole pointed to Robbie's performance

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:02.360
as a merciful exception.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.400
The Chicago Tribune's Michael Phillips, for
example, wrote:

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:10.280
"Robbie is radioactively watchable, swinging
her baseball bat this way and that, selling

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.680
this skeezy male-fantasy nutjob with wide-eyed
enthusiasm."

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.440
In early 2018, DC Comics announced the launch
of its Black Label imprint.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:23.920
DC Black Label promised to give premiere talent
the opportunity to tell standalone, mature-readers

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.100
stories outside of the current DC Universe
continuity.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.400
This freedom allows creators to tell exactly
the stories they want to tell without worrying

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.280
about impacting the broader DC Comics Universe.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.120
And as you might've guessed, Harley Quinn
has already proven to be the star of two of

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.320
the imprint's miniseries: Harleen and Joker/Harley:
Criminal Sanity.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.880
Joker/Harley: Criminal Sanity, by writer Kami
Garcia, reframes Harley's origin completely.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.360
Instead of beginning her comic book life as
Joker's doctor in Arkham Asylum, the Harley

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:56.660
of Criminal Sanity is a criminal profiler
assisting the Gotham Police Department in

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:57.780
tracking down a killer.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:02.910
Meanwhile, Stjepan Šejić's Harleen offers
the more familiar Dr. Harleen Quinzel of Arkham

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:07.070
Asylum but refuses to take her relationship
with the Joker for granted.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:11.600
Instead, Šejić takes readers on a slow-burn,
intriguing trip, in order to show exactly

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.540
how the flawed Dr. Quinzel could become so
tragically obsessed with the Joker.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.140
In February 2020, fans will finally get the
chance to see Margot Robbie reprise the role

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:25.810
of Harley in Birds of Prey (and the Fantabulous
Emancipation of One Harley Quinn).

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:30.050
The film takes place after a bad break up
between Harley and the Joker, and like the

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:34.110
DC Universe animated series Harley Quinn,
the anti-heroine is now on a quest to make

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.190
her own way in the world.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.960
Along the way, she's joined by a number of
mainstays from DC's mythos— such as Jurnee

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:44.790
Smollett-Bell's Black Canary, Mary Elizabeth
Winstead's Huntress, Rosie Perez's former

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.680
Gotham cop Renee Montoya, and Ella Jay Basco's
Cassandra Cain.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.100
Joker doesn't appear in the film in person,
though.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:56.000
Instead, Harley and her new allies face Ewan
McGregor's maniacal crime lord Black Mask.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.630
The Birds of Prey have had a number of series
over the years, and they even had their own

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.120
short-lived television series in the early
aughts.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.040
But Harley's addition to the movie team and
her prominence in the line-up is one of the

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.500
biggest departures from the Birds of Prey
comics.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.300
On the page, she really has nothing to do
with the crew at all.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.380
Now though, just like with Suicide Squad,
her name is pretty much inseparable from the

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:15.880
brand.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.940
Harley Quinn is taking over the world.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.590
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.340
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
anti-heroes are coming soon.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.460
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

